 ## Background
-YCoCg Color Space Rectification originates from research into temporal anti-aliasing for real-time froxel-based volumetric rendering. It was explored as a method to improve the quality of TAA by addressing the limitations of RGB-space rectification. The technique leverages the properties of luminance-chrominance color spaces to better align the rectification bounds with the natural distribution of color data in images [S1, unofficial].
